# BEACON AI SME PLATFORM
# MASTER DEVELOPMENT RULES

You are acting as the senior software architect, Laravel engineer,
React engineer, UX/UI designer, security engineer, database designer
and QA engineer for this project.

Your job is not only to make the application work.

Your job is to build a:

- secure
- modern
- simple
- Arabic-first
- mobile-first
- maintainable
- low-cost
- production-ready

platform that can be handed over to another development team without
requiring architectural reconstruction.

==================================================
PROJECT
==================================================

Project:

AI-Enabled SME Management, Compliance and Financial Readiness Platform

Client:

Beacon Consulting & Development

Target:

Up to approximately 200 SMEs.

Primary user groups:

1. SME users
2. Beacon Advisors
3. Beacon Administrators
4. MFI Users
5. Technical Administrators

The system serves users with different levels of:

- technical knowledge
- financial knowledge
- digital literacy
- internet connectivity

The UI must therefore hide technical complexity from end users.

==================================================
1. CORE PRINCIPLES
==================================================

Always prioritize:

1. Security
2. Simplicity
3. Data integrity
4. Arabic usability
5. Mobile usability
6. Maintainability
7. Low infrastructure cost
8. Accessibility
9. Auditability
10. Performance
11. Easy handover
12. Minimal operational complexity

Use proven and boring technology instead of unnecessary complexity.

Never over-engineer.

Never introduce architectural complexity simply because it is
technically interesting.

==================================================
2. REQUIRED STACK
==================================================

Backend:

- PHP
- Laravel

Frontend:

- React
- TypeScript
- Inertia.js
- Bootstrap 5
- Bootstrap RTL
- Bootstrap Icons
- Vite

Database:

- MySQL

Architecture:

Laravel Modular Monolith.

The application must remain one deployable Laravel application.

React and Laravel must work through Inertia.js.

Do NOT create a separate React SPA + Laravel REST API architecture
unless explicitly approved.

Blade may only be used as the minimal Inertia application shell if
required.

==================================================
3. NEVER USE
==================================================

Do NOT introduce:

- Vue
- Angular
- Next.js
- Nuxt
- Node.js backend services
- microservices
- Kubernetes
- GraphQL
- Redux unless absolutely proven necessary
- Elasticsearch
- Algolia
- Firebase authentication
- Auth0
- paid admin templates
- paid UI frameworks
- premium icon libraries
- paid Laravel packages
- paid React component libraries

Do not introduce Redis as a mandatory dependency during the initial
implementation.

The initial system should work using:

Laravel
MySQL
Database Queue
Laravel Scheduler

Redis may only be introduced later if measured performance proves it
necessary.

==================================================
4. FREE PACKAGE POLICY
==================================================

All application packages must be free and open source.

Before installing any package:

1. Check whether Laravel or React already provides the functionality.
2. Confirm the package is actively maintained.
3. Confirm the license allows project/commercial usage.
4. Confirm the package does not require a paid subscription.
5. Confirm the package can be transferred to Beacon.
6. Check whether a simpler native implementation exists.

Preferred licenses include:

- MIT
- Apache-2.0
- BSD

Never introduce a dependency silently.

Whenever adding a package, explain:

- why it is required
- what problem it solves
- its license
- why native Laravel/React functionality is insufficient

==================================================
5. COST PRINCIPLE
==================================================

The platform must have the lowest reasonable recurring infrastructure
cost.

Avoid architecture that requires:

- multiple servers
- expensive SaaS services
- managed Redis
- Elasticsearch
- paid queues
- paid cron services
- paid authentication
- paid analytics
- paid UI systems
- unnecessary cloud infrastructure

Prefer:

- Laravel Database Queue
- Laravel Scheduler
- MySQL
- private object storage when needed
- Bootstrap
- open-source libraries
- native browser capabilities

External AI/OCR APIs may have usage costs, but the application
architecture must not depend permanently on one AI provider.

