==================================================
9. RESPONSIVE APPLICATION STRATEGY
==================================================

THIS IS A CRITICAL PROJECT RULE.

The system must feel like TWO EXPERIENCES using ONE codebase:

MOBILE:
must feel like a native mobile application.

DESKTOP:
must feel like a professional web application.

Do NOT create a separate mobile application.

Do NOT create a second frontend codebase.

Use responsive React components and layouts.

==================================================
10. MOBILE EXPERIENCE
==================================================

On smartphones, the application must visually behave like a mobile
app rather than a shrunk desktop website.

Target widths:

360px
375px
390px
412px
430px

Use mobile-first design.

For widths below the Bootstrap `lg` breakpoint, use the mobile
application shell.

The mobile experience should include:

- full viewport application layout
- mobile app header
- bottom navigation
- large touch targets
- card-based information
- simple lists instead of wide tables
- mobile-friendly forms
- sticky actions where useful
- bottom sheets or Bootstrap offcanvas for secondary actions
- minimal visual clutter

Do NOT display the desktop sidebar on mobile.

==================================================
11. MOBILE APP HEADER
==================================================

Create a reusable component such as:

MobileAppHeader

The mobile header may contain:

- page title
- back button
- notification button
- profile/avatar button
- contextual action when appropriate

Keep the header compact.

Recommended height:

56px to 64px.

Do not overload the mobile header.

==================================================
12. MOBILE BOTTOM NAVIGATION
==================================================

On mobile, use fixed bottom navigation.

Create reusable component:

MobileBottomNavigation

Use maximum:

4 or 5 main navigation destinations.

Example SME navigation:

الرئيسية
المعاملات
التقارير
الجاهزية
المزيد

The "More" section may contain:

الامتثال
المستندات
المساعد
الإحالات
حسابي

Do not place 8+ buttons in the bottom navigation.

Each navigation item must contain:

- icon
- Arabic text label

Never use icon-only bottom navigation.

The active item must be obvious.

Bottom navigation must respect:

safe-area-inset-bottom

on supported mobile devices.

Content must include enough bottom padding so navigation never covers
page content.

==================================================
13. MOBILE TOUCH TARGETS
==================================================

Interactive mobile controls should have comfortable touch sizes.

Aim for a minimum touch target around:

44x44px

Primary mobile buttons should normally be at least:

44px to 48px high.

Avoid tiny icons and small clickable text.

==================================================
14. MOBILE FORMS
==================================================

Mobile forms must feel like application workflows.

Use:

- full-width inputs
- large input height
- clear labels
- step-by-step flows
- sticky save/next button where appropriate
- progress indicators for long workflows

Do not present 20-30 fields at once.

Break long workflows into logical steps.

Example:

الخطوة 1 من 4

Use clear next/back actions.

==================================================
15. MOBILE TABLE RULE
==================================================

Do not display unreadable desktop tables on smartphones.

For mobile:

Convert important table rows into cards or structured list items.

Example transaction card:

مصروف
250,000 ل.س
12 أكتوبر 2026

تصنيف:
مواصلات

الحالة:
مكتمل

Desktop may use a table.

Mobile should use a card/list representation when this improves
readability.

==================================================
16. MOBILE PRIMARY ACTION
==================================================

Important screens may use a floating or sticky primary action.

Examples:

+ إضافة معاملة

رفع فاتورة

إضافة مستند

Do not use floating actions unnecessarily.

There must never be multiple competing floating actions.

==================================================
17. MOBILE MODALS
==================================================

Prefer:

Bootstrap offcanvas / bottom-sheet-style interaction

for mobile secondary actions.

Examples:

Filters
Record actions
More menu
Details

Large desktop modal dialogs should not simply shrink into tiny mobile
windows.

==================================================
18. MOBILE DASHBOARD
==================================================

The SME mobile dashboard should answer:

"What should I do next?"

Priority order:

1. important action / alert
2. current financial summary
3. missing information
4. compliance action
5. readiness progress
6. latest transactions
7. additional information

Avoid chart-heavy mobile dashboards.

Cards should be vertically stacked.

==================================================
19. MOBILE NAVIGATION BEHAVIOR
==================================================

The user should feel they are navigating between application screens,
not browsing traditional web pages.

Use Inertia navigation.

Avoid unnecessary full-page reloads.

Maintain predictable back navigation.

Do not use excessive animations.

Subtle transitions are acceptable only if they improve clarity.

==================================================
20. DESKTOP WEB APPLICATION
==================================================

At the Bootstrap `lg` breakpoint and above, switch to a professional
desktop web application layout.

Desktop layout:

------------------------------------------------
| Sidebar | Topbar                            |
|         |-----------------------------------|
|         |                                   |
|         | Main Content Area                 |
|         |                                   |
------------------------------------------------

Use:

DesktopSidebar
DesktopTopbar
DesktopAppLayout

Do NOT display mobile bottom navigation on desktop.

==================================================
21. DESKTOP SIDEBAR
==================================================

Desktop sidebar should be:

- clean
- compact
- easy to scan
- grouped by workflow

Recommended width:

240px to 280px

Allow collapse if useful.

Do not create dozens of visible menu items.

Group related areas.

Example SME:

الرئيسية

المالية
- المعاملات
- التقارير

الجاهزية والامتثال
- الامتثال
- الجاهزية
- الإحالات

المستندات

المساعد

Desktop admins can receive additional sections.

==================================================
22. DESKTOP CONTENT
==================================================

Desktop pages may use:

- cards
- responsive grids
- data tables
- charts
- side panels

Do not stretch forms across the full screen.

Recommended readable form widths:

approximately 650px to 900px depending on context.

Use wider layouts primarily for:

- reports
- dashboards
- administrative tables

==================================================
23. SINGLE COMPONENT SYSTEM
==================================================

Mobile and desktop must share:

- business logic
- permissions
- validation
- API/backend
- routes
- state where practical

Avoid duplicating whole pages.

Prefer responsive components.

Example:

<TransactionList>

could internally render:

DesktopTransactionTable

or:

MobileTransactionCards

depending on layout.

==================================================
24. PWA
==================================================

The application should be designed so it can behave as an installable
Progressive Web App.

PWA support is a progressive enhancement.

Use only free/open-source tooling.

Provide:

- web app manifest
- application name
- icons
- theme color
- standalone display mode

When installed on a phone:

display mode should preferably be:

standalone

so the platform opens without normal browser chrome where supported.

Do NOT attempt to cache the entire application offline.

==================================================
25. OFFLINE SUPPORT
==================================================

Offline functionality must be limited to approved selected forms.

Examples:

- field draft forms
- selected SME data collection

Do not implement full offline financial processing.

Never finalize:

- financial posting
- MFI referrals
- AI operations

while offline.

Offline records must have explicit status:

مسودة محلية

بانتظار المزامنة

تمت المزامنة

تعارض يحتاج مراجعة

Never silently overwrite server data.

==================================================
26. OFFLINE SYNCHRONIZATION
==================================================

Synchronization must:

1. re-authenticate/verify session
2. recheck authorization
3. revalidate data
4. detect duplicates
5. detect server-side changes
6. detect conflicts
7. avoid silent overwriting

Use a client-generated UUID where appropriate for offline drafts to
prevent duplicate submissions.

==================================================
27. UI DESIGN LANGUAGE
==================================================

The interface should feel:

- modern
- professional
- calm
- minimal
- friendly
- trustworthy

Do NOT create:

- flashy startup UI
- gaming UI
- excessive gradients
- glassmorphism
- neon styling
- excessive animations
- huge shadows
- decorative clutter

The platform should feel like a modern financial/business application.

