}

Use consistent:

- spacing
- border radius
- button size
- input size
- typography
- card styles

Never invent a different style for every page.

==================================================
29. BEACON BRANDING
==================================================

Use Beacon branding conservatively.

Brand colors should primarily appear in:

- logo
- navigation active state
- primary buttons
- important links
- selected highlights

Do not paint entire pages in strong brand colors.

Keep content surfaces mostly:

white
off-white
light neutral backgrounds.

==================================================
30. ARABIC FIRST
==================================================

Arabic is the default interface.

Root application should support:

lang="ar"
dir="rtl"

Use Bootstrap RTL.

Do not manually fake RTL.

Also support English LTR.

All components must work with:

- Arabic
- English
- mixed Arabic/English
- Western digits
- Arabic digits where applicable

==================================================
31. CSS DIRECTION RULE
==================================================

Prefer logical CSS properties.

Prefer:

margin-inline-start
margin-inline-end
padding-inline-start
padding-inline-end
inset-inline-start

Avoid hard-coding:

margin-left
margin-right

when logical CSS can solve both RTL and LTR.

==================================================
32. TYPOGRAPHY
==================================================

Arabic readability is more important than decorative design.

Use a clean free/open-source Arabic-compatible font or reliable system
font stack.

Never introduce paid fonts.

Recommended sizes:

Page title:
24px-28px desktop
20px-24px mobile

Section heading:
18px-22px

Body:
15px-16px

Secondary:
13px-14px minimum

Input text:
16px minimum on mobile

Avoid extremely light font weight.

==================================================
33. REACT RULES
==================================================

Use:

- React functional components
- TypeScript
- reusable components
- small focused components

Avoid giant 1000-line components.

Separate:

presentation
business interaction
server logic

Laravel remains authoritative for business rules.

React handles:

- rendering
- interaction
- client-side usability
- temporary UI state

==================================================
34. REACT STATE
==================================================

Prefer:

- Inertia props
- local useState
- useMemo where useful
- small custom hooks

Do not introduce Redux unless there is a real application-wide state
problem that cannot be solved cleanly otherwise.

Do not add React Query automatically.

Do not manually fetch all Laravel pages via Axios if normal Inertia
requests solve the use case.

==================================================
35. INERTIA
==================================================

Use Inertia for normal application navigation.

Use Inertia Forms for standard CRUD workflows when appropriate.

Laravel validation remains authoritative.

React validation may help UX but must never replace server validation.

